---
title: Auth - Register Flow (POST /auth/register)
---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Client
    participant Ctrl as AuthController
    participant Service as AuthService
    participant AccSvc as AccountsService
    participant AccountModel as AccountModel (TypeORM Repository)
    participant CustomerModel as CustomerModel (TypeORM Repository)
    participant Util as Security Utils (bcrypt / crypto / jwt)
    participant DB as Database (SQL Server)

    note right of Client: POST /auth/register
    Client->>Ctrl: RegisterDto (username, fullName, email, phone, password)
    Ctrl->>Service: register(dto)
    Service->>AccountModel: findOne({ username })
    AccountModel->>DB: SELECT * FROM Accounts WHERE Username = ?
    DB-->>AccountModel: row / null
    AccountModel-->>Service: account / null
    opt Username exists
        Service-->>Client: Throw ConflictException
    end
    Service->>Util: bcrypt.hash(password, 10)
    Util-->>Service: passwordHash
    Service->>AccSvc: create(username, passwordHash)
    AccSvc->>AccountModel: save(account)
    AccountModel->>DB: INSERT INTO Accounts ...
    DB-->>AccountModel: persisted row
    AccountModel-->>AccSvc: Account Entity
    AccSvc-->>Service: Account Entity
    Service->>AccSvc: setRole(accountId, 'User')
    AccSvc->>AccountModel: save(role)
    AccountModel->>DB: UPDATE Accounts SET Role = 'User' WHERE AccountId = ?
    DB-->>AccountModel: ok
    Service->>CustomerModel: save(customer)
    CustomerModel->>DB: INSERT INTO Customers ...
    DB-->>CustomerModel: persisted row
    CustomerModel-->>Service: Customer Entity
    Service-->>Ctrl: RegisterResponseDto (message, customerId)
    Ctrl-->>Client: HTTP 201 - RegisterResponseDto